<title>SWITZERLAND: Bank Baer raises end-97 SPI target to 2,900 points.</title>
<headline>Bank Baer raises end-97 SPI target to 2,900 points.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Julius Baer said it lifted its target for the all-share Swiss Performance Index to 2,900 points from 2,800 to reflect higher earnings estimates stemming from currency gains on the weak Swiss franc.</p>
<p>&quot;As a result of the currency-induced five percent increase in our earnings estimates, we have raised our price target for the SPI to end-1997 from 2,800 to 2,900 SPI points,&quot; it said it its latest Market View Switzerland publication.</p>
<p>The SPI was around 2,862 points at midday.</p>
<p>It continued to recommend overweighting the lagging banking and insurance sectors, particularly Swiss Bank Corp, Zurich Insurance and Swiss Re.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
